Installing Vaigil
*****************

From source, or from a release: a signed binary or a container image.  No
release is published yet, so build it from source.


From source
===========

Requirements
------------

Go 1.27 or later.  Nothing else.

This is a Go program with no dependencies: `go.mod` has no require block, so
the standard library and the Go toolchain are the whole build.  There is no
`./configure`, because there is nothing to configure at build time.


Building and installing
-----------------------

     make
     sudo make install

`make install` honours the usual variables:

     sudo make install prefix=/usr/local     # the default
     make install prefix="$HOME/.local"      # no root needed
     sudo make install DESTDIR=/tmp/stage    # for a package build

To remove it:

     sudo make uninstall


Without make
------------

     go build -o vaigil ./cmd/vaigil
     install -m 0755 vaigil /usr/local/bin/


A container from source
-----------------------

     docker build -t vaigil .
     docker run --rm -v vaigil:/srv vaigil --root /srv/store init --admin you@example.com
     docker run -p 8080:8080 -v vaigil:/srv vaigil

The first command prints the link that adds your passkey; open it once the
second is running.

The base is `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot`: the binary, CA
certificates, a passwd entry and timezone data.  No shell, no package manager,
no interpreter, no libc.  It runs as nonroot, and carries LICENSE and NOTICE in
/usr/share/doc/vaigil.


From a release
==============

Each release publishes one static binary for each of linux, macOS and Windows
on amd64 and arm64, with SHA256SUMS, LICENSE and NOTICE beside them, and a
container image, ghcr.io/vaigil/vaigil, tagged with the version without its
`v`: the git tag v1.2.3 publishes 1.2.3, 1.2 and latest.

Check a binary before you run it:

     sha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS
     gh attestation verify vaigil-linux-amd64 --repo Vaigil/Vaigil

The checksum proves the file matches the list.  The attestation proves the
file was built by this repository's release workflow, from a tag, and names
which one.


Checking the build
==================

     make check

That runs the whole test suite: seventy packages, including several that walk
this program's own source and fail when a command has no screen or no machine
interface without a written reason, or declares no privilege.

A test counts the packages and fails naming the right number when this one is
wrong.


A first run
===========

     vaigil init --admin you@example.com
     vaigil serve

Then open the link `init` printed, add a passkey, and follow Get started.


